From: Craig Johnson <1545411+captainpacket@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 19:04:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] plugin: document endpoint-scoped koko locking

Keep the meshnet CNI call-site contract aligned with koko: actors sharing an endpoint serialize, while disjoint same-node wires may now progress concurrently.
---
 plugin/meshnet.go | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/plugin/meshnet.go b/plugin/meshnet.go
index ecd3e9f..1cbc083 100644
--- a/plugin/meshnet.go
+++ b/plugin/meshnet.go
@@ -557,7 +557,8 @@ func cmdAdd(args *skel.CmdArgs) (retErr error) {
 
 				// Idempotently realize the wire. Both directions of a link may
 				// attempt this concurrently (both pods' ADDs); koko serializes
-				// all wire creators node-wide and either adopts a wire the
+				// creators sharing either endpoint while allowing disjoint
+				// wires to progress concurrently. It either adopts a wire the
 				// peer already realized correctly, replaces stale halves, or
 				// fails loudly when a different wire owns the name. This
 				// replaces the old check-then-MakeVeth branches, whose
